  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Counter Ticket (فیش و شماره)",
    "overview": "Ordering at Kiloechi works like ordering at an Iranian fast-food counter. You take a slip, your number lights up on the red-and-black call board, and it is called hot. The site refuses the delivery-app default of a split photo hero over a row of equal product cards. Its parts are the counter's own: a near-black call board with yellow LED readouts across the top of every page, thermal slips with torn edges that hold the menu, red rubber stamps that land when something changes, and status lamps that light one by one.\n\nPublic pages (home, menu) persuade on a saturated fryer-red field. Working screens (cart, checkout, account, admin) keep the same materials but quieter, with paper on red for customers and a cool counter grey for staff. Everything shown on the board is true: the visitor's own order number and status, or today's real count of discounted dishes, never invented numbers.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "The board is the horizon of every page: sticky, edge to edge, a dot grille behind yellow dot-matrix numerals.",
      "One slip row is the ruler for every dish on every page (photo, name, description, price, add control).",
      "Red stamps appear only on state change: discounted, added, delivered, cancelled.",
      "The added dish lifts forward and prints a new line onto \"your slip\".",
      "Persian right-to-left throughout, Persian digits, Toman prices, Solar Hijri dates."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Yellow-on-Red Rule",
        "body": "Yellow sits on red only at display size (the hero headline). Every other yellow text sits on board black.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Cream Ban Rule",
        "body": "Paper is thermal white `#fdfdfb` and the admin ground is cool `#eceeee`. Warm cream grounds are out.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One LED Face Rule",
        "body": "Numbers that are live data (counts, order numbers, quantities) are Handjet dot-matrix. Prices are Vazirmatn with tabular figures, because they are printed, not lit.",
        "section": "typography"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do show only true data on the board and in the footer; hide what the owner hasn't provided.",
      "Do keep every dish in the same slip row, on every page.",
      "Do mark discounts on the price itself: struck old price plus a red stamp.",
      "Do keep tap targets at least 44px and focus rings visible (yellow on dark and red, deep red on paper).",
      "Do respect `prefers-reduced-motion`: no lift, press or feed movement; fades only."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use emoji or Unicode glyphs as icons; use the 2px-stroke SVG set in `components/Icons.jsx`.",
      "Don't invent testimonials, branches, ratings, order numbers or prices.",
      "Don't put yellow text on red below display size.",
      "Don't use warm cream grounds, gradient text, glass effects, or thick one-side accent borders.",
      "Don't add a generic numbered \"how it works\" strip; the status lamps tell that story."
    ]
  }
}